    {
      "id": "HI-C70-game",
      "sequence": 2930,
      "title": "खेल (khel) — a game",
      "headword": "खेल",
      "romanization": "khel",
      "gloss": "a game",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:0f8a081dbda17263",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words back: what does ṭikaṭ mean, and what is जाना? The next five words are what you do when you are not going anywhere."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: खेल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खेल (khel) — \"a game\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit खेल (khela), \"play, sport\", from a root that meant shaking or moving about. The final vowel dropped away by the schwa rule and left the bare consonant ending Hindi likes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खेल (khel) covers more than a sport with rules. A child's game is a खेल (khel), a match is a खेल (khel), and a thing somebody is not taking seriously is a खेल (khel) too. When somebody you have just met asks what you do with your evenings, this is the word the answer starts from."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ख is the aspirated one — a real puff of breath after the k, which is what separates खेल (khel) from क, and the difference changes the word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five words for the hours after work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say ṭikaṭ, then read जाना and say what it means",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *ṭikaṭ*, then read **जाना** and say what it means]"
