    {
      "id": "HI-C70-cricket",
      "sequence": 2950,
      "title": "क्रिकेट (krikeṭ) — cricket, the game",
      "headword": "क्रिकेट",
      "romanization": "krikeṭ",
      "gloss": "cricket, the game",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:5fa9336e2278a1ed",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which of your two words is the game, and which is the doing word made out of it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: क्रिकेट",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क्रिकेट (krikeṭ) — \"cricket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English, borrowed whole, and written with two things you have already met. The opening क्र is क stacked on र by the same vowel-killer ् that stacks स्ट in स्टेशन. The final ट is retroflex, because an English t always lands there."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ि after the stack is the short i matra, and it sits to the left of the whole cluster even though it is sounded after it — the same preposed matra you first met in a name."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "If you learn one game word in Hindi, learn this one. मैं क्रिकेट (krikeṭ) खेलता हूँ puts three of this chapter's ideas into a single sentence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three: खेल, खेलना (khelnā), क्रिकेट (krikeṭ). A game, playing it, and one to name."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "READ",
              "instruction": "क्रिकेट (krikeṭ), and find the ि sitting to the left of the stack",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU READ: क्रिकेट, and find the ि sitting to the left of the stack]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "krikeṭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *krikeṭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "maiṁ krikeṭ kheltā hūṁ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *maiṁ krikeṭ kheltā hūṁ*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does क्रिकेट (krikeṭ) mean? (\"cricket\".) Say that you play it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HI-C70-song",
      "sequence": 2960,
      "title": "गाना (gānā) — a song",
      "headword": "गाना",
      "romanization": "gānā",
      "gloss": "a song",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "sight",
      "derivedModality": "sight",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "sight-cue"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:5041a8a2e393bfca",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "sight",
        "needs": [
          "your eyes, because the lesson points at something written down"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Guided Practice"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your eyes, so it is not fully a driving lesson. You will want your eyes, because the lesson points at something written down. You can listen to everything else now — leave the section called Guided Practice until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Write क्रिकेट (krikeṭ) from memory, starting with the ि you put down first."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: गाना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गाना (gānā) — \"a song\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit गान (gāna), \"singing\", from गै (gai-), \"to sing\". The root is one of the oldest in the language and it has never stopped working."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now notice the shape. गाना (gānā) ends in -ना, exactly like खेलना (khelnā) — and that is not an accident. गाना (gānā) is also the doing word \"to sing\". One spelling, two jobs: the song, and the singing of it. Which one is meant is settled by the sentence around it and never by the word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hindi does this often enough that it is worth expecting rather than being surprised by. You will meet another word with the same double life before this run of chapters is out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four, and the first word you have met that is two words at once."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "gānā",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *gānā*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "CONTRAST",
              "instruction": "gānā as the song, and gānā as the singing",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU CONTRAST: *gānā* as the song, and *gānā* as the singing]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "गाना (gānā), then खेलना (khelnā) under it, and look at the ending they share",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: गाना, then खेलना under it, and look at the ending they share]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What two things can गाना (gānā) mean? (\"a song\", and \"to sing\".)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
