              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Name the four words of this chapter so far."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आराम",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आराम (ārām) — \"rest, ease\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Persian آرام (ārām), \"quiet, calm, repose\". It came in with the Persian half of the vocabulary and settled deep: आरामकुर्सी is an easy chair, built from आराम and the कुर्सी you already own."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आराम (ārām) is not sleep. नींद is sleep, and you have that word. आराम (ārām) is the state of not being pushed — sitting down, breathing out, nothing owed to anybody for an hour. आराम (ārām) करना is what you say for taking that hour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is also an answer. When somebody asks आप कैसे हैं?, one ordinary reply is that you are at आराम (ārām), and it says more warmly than ठीक does."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: खेल, खेलना (khelnā), क्रिकेट (krikeṭ), गाना (gānā), आराम (ārām). Enough to say what you do when the day lets go of you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
